@startuml
title SPI mode 3 + per-word CRC — the master engine, as the code has it
' Sources: firmware/spi_mode3.pe (dmem[10] chain, bit_loop, fold_byte),
'          tb/tb_pe_soc_spi3.v (the mode-3 slave model, the pin-discipline
'          monitors, the reference CRC-8), tools/fw/peasm.py (TICKS_PER_BIT)
' Program: CS_N v | WORD(16) | CRC8(WORD)(8) | RESP(8) | CRC8(RESP)(8) | CS_N ^
'          three words: 0x1134 0x1245 0x1356, one CS_N frame each
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam state {
  FontSize 11
  BackgroundColor<<tx>>   #dce9f8
  BorderColor<<tx>>       #4a6fa5
  FontColor<<tx>>         #16324f
  BackgroundColor<<rx>>   #dceee0
  BorderColor<<rx>>       #4a8a5c
  FontColor<<rx>>         #17452a
  BackgroundColor<<crc>>  #fbe9cf
  BorderColor<<crc>>      #b8813a
  FontColor<<crc>>        #5a3d12
  BackgroundColor<<box>>  #f2f2f2
  BorderColor<<box>>      #808080
  FontColor<<box>>        #303030
}

state "BUS FSM — dmem[10]\nthe chain is POSITIONAL: each branch tests the state one\nlower than the branch above, so a missing state does not\nbecome unreachable, it SHIFTS every state above it" as bus <<box>>
state "0\nCS_N low, assemble\nword 0x1134+i" as s0
state "1\nshift out the\nHIGH byte" as s1 <<tx>>
state "2\nshift out the\nLOW byte" as s2 <<tx>>
state "3\nfold CRC-8 over\nboth bytes" as s3 <<crc>>
state "4\nshift out\nthe CRC-8" as s4 <<tx>>
state "5\nreceive 8 bits\n-> dmem[1]" as s5 <<rx>>
state "6\nstore it, fold\nCRC-8 over it" as s6 <<crc>>
state "7\nreceive 8 bits\n-> dmem[2]" as s7 <<rx>>
state "8\ncompare, record,\nCS_N high" as s8
state "9\npark\ndmem[15]=0xA5" as s9
state "dispatch\nmain: LDM A,10\nSUB A,1 / JZ" as dsp <<box>>

[*] --> dsp
dsp --> s0
s0 --> s1
s1 --> s2
s2 --> s3
s3 --> s4
s4 --> s5
s5 --> s6
s6 --> s7
s7 --> s8
s8 --> dsp : dmem[5] < 3
s8 --> s9 : dmem[5] == 3

state "bit_loop — ONE mode-3 cell, full duplex\nentered and left with SCLK HIGH\ndmem[8] out, dmem[10] count, dmem[11] acc, dmem[12] return state" as bleng <<box>> {
  state "1. LAUNCH\nMOSI while SCLK is HIGH\nout = 1 or 0 on bit 1;\ndmem[8] <<= 1" as b1 <<tx>>
  state "2. FALL\nSCL low — the only moment\nMISO may change" as b2
  state "3. WAIT\nsnapshot TIMER into X,\npoll until it changes\n(260 clocks = 4.3333 us)" as b3
  state "4. RISE + SAMPLE\nSCL high: the slave captures MOSI\nIN A,PIN / AND A,8 reads MISO\nacc = acc*2 + bit" as b4 <<rx>>
  b1 --> b2
  b2 --> b3
  b3 --> b4
  b4 --> b1 : dmem[10]-- , 8 cells per byte
}

state "fold_byte — CRC-8 in an ISA with no XOR\ndmem[14] = crc, dmem[13] = input byte,\ndmem[3] = bytes left" as fold <<crc>> {
  state "MSB first, 8 times per byte:\nV = 0x80 test, P = poly 0x07 if set\nXOR as (A|P) - (A&P):\n  0xFF + 0x07 = 0x06, but\n  0xFF XOR 0x07 = 0xF8,\n  so ADD cannot be used" as f1 <<crc>>
}

state "JMP bit_loop\nstates 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 all enter here" as blcall
s0 --> blcall
s1 --> blcall
s2 --> blcall
s4 --> blcall
s5 --> blcall
s7 --> blcall
blcall --> bleng
bleng --> dsp : bl_done -> dmem[10] = dmem[12]
s3 --> fold
s6 --> fold
fold --> s4
fold --> s7

note right of s8
  dmem[5]  words transmitted
  dmem[6]  response CRCs that CHECKED OUT
  dmem[7]  the last word's transmitted CRC-8
  The comparison is on the firmware's own
  side of the wire: recompute CRC-8(RESP)
  in software and compare with the byte
  that came back. A program that never
  compared, or that always incremented,
  reports 3 of 3 — so the TB corrupts one
  response CRC on purpose and demands 2.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title SPI mode 3 — one CS_N frame is 40 SCLK rises, in four fields
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #eef3fb
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #4a6fa5
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #16324f
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #fbe9cf
skinparam ActorBorderColor #b8813a
skinparam ActorFontColor #5a3d12
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #fbfbfb
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #b0b0b0
skinparam ArrowColor #333333

actor "master\npe_soc" as M
participant "SCLK\nbit 0" as C
participant "MOSI\nbit 1" as O
participant "MISO\nbit 3" as I
actor "slave\ndecodes the pins" as S

M -> C : CS_N (bit 2) 1 -> 0
M -> C : SCLK idles HIGH — the reset level happens to be 1
group WORD — 16 rises, MOSI MSB first
  M -> O : rise 0..7   0001 0001   = 0x11
  S -> I : MISO idle LOW for rises 0..23
  M -> O : rise 8..15  0011 0100   = 0x34
  note over O
    measured on the wire: word = 1134.
    0x1134 is not a bit palindrome - its
    reversal is 0x3411 - so a master that
    shifted the other way is visible.
  end note
end group
group CRC8(WORD) — 8 rises, the transmit-side integrity check
  M -> O : rise 16..23  1100 1110   = 0xCE
  note over S
    the slave recomputes CRC-8 over the 16
    bits it decoded and requires it to equal
    these 8. A reference datapath written in
    Verilog straight from the polynomial says
    the same thing: a CRC checked against
    itself proves nothing.
  end note
end group
group RESP — 8 rises, MISO MSB first
  S -> I : rise 24..31  0110 1111   = 0x6F
  note over I
    resp = word XOR 0x7E5A, applied
    byte-wise by the slave model.
  end note
end group
group CRC8(RESP) — 8 rises, the receive-side check
  S -> I : rise 32..39  0000 1010   = 0x0A
  note over M
    the firmware recomputes this in
    software and compares. Exactly 40
    rises: a master that clocked 39 or 41
    would still shift plausible bytes.
  end note
end group
M -> C : CS_N 0 -> 1

note over M, S
  MODE 3 IS NOT MODE 0 WITH THE CLOCK INVERTED.  Both modes sample on the
  RISING edge, so a mode-0 program is a plausible-looking mode-3 program for
  the first half-frame and then delivers bit k-1 as bit k — shifted by one,
  with nothing on the wire that looks wrong. The two things that catch it are
  a slave that decodes the pins, and the check on the IDLE LEVEL.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title SPI mode 3 — the two edges are the protocol, and they are the same in both directions
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #eef3fb
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #4a6fa5
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #16324f
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #fbfbfb
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #b0b0b0
skinparam ArrowColor #333333

actor "master" as M
participant "SCLK" as C #fbe9cf
participant "MOSI\nmaster drives" as O
participant "MISO\nslave drives" as I
actor "slave" as S #dceee0

M -> C : SCLK HIGH (mode 3 idle)
M -> O : launch bit k  — data changes while the clock is HIGH
M -> C : SCLK FALLS
S -> I : the only instant MISO may change
M -> C : SCLK RISES  (one TIMER tick later)
S -> O : the slave CAPTURES MOSI here
M -> I : the master SAMPLES MISO here
note over O, I
  MOSI MUST NOT MOVE WHILE SCL IS LOW
  MISO MUST NOT MOVE WHILE SCL IS HIGH
  Two counters in the TB, both asserted 0.
  They are the checks a mode-0 program fails
  even when the decoded bytes happen to be
  right — which is exactly the case a byte
  comparison cannot see.
end note
note over C
  IDLE LEVEL ALONE DOES NOT SEPARATE THE MODES.
  Reset already drives the output register's
  bit 0 HIGH, which is mode 3's idle clock by
  coincidence and mode 0's ACTIVE edge by
  construction. The property that does separate
  them is an EDGE: in mode 3 SCLK must make no
  falling edge at all while CS_N is high.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
!pragma teoz
title SPI mode 3 — one bit cell: 5 phases over one measured 4.367 us = 262 clocks
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
robust "label" as F
concise "SCLK" as C
concise "MOSI" as O
concise "nums" as N
@0
F is bl_launch
C is 1
O is "bit 7"
N is "CPOL=1"
@6
F is bl_fall
C is 0
N is "the FALL"
@12
F is bl_wait
N is "wait 260"
@18
F is bl_rise
C is 1
N is "the RISE"
@24
F is bl_sample
O is "bit 6"
C is 0
N is "sample"
@30
N is "4.367 us"
@36
N is "< 21.67 us"
@endsync
@enduml

@startuml
!pragma teoz
title SPI mode 3 — one CS_N frame, 40 rises, 4 fields; the axis counts RISES, not time
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
robust "slave field" as F
concise "CS_N" as CS
concise "rises" as R
concise "wire" as W
concise "the bytes" as B
@0
F is idle
CS is 1
W is "MISO low"
B is "deselected"
@1
F is word
CS is 0
R is "0..15"
W is "MOSI"
B is "0x1134"
@16
F is crc_in
R is "16..23"
B is "0xCE"
@24
F is resp
R is "24..31"
W is "MISO"
B is "0x6F"
@32
F is crc_resp
R is "32..39"
B is "0x0A"
@40
F is next_word
CS is 1
W is "MISO low"
B is "40 rises"
@41
R is "40"
B is "CS_N high"
@46
B is "no SCLK fall here"
@52
F is word
CS is 0
B is "next frame"
@58
B is "3 words, 120 rises"
@endsync
@enduml
